# Day 4 – Ultrasonic Sensor

## Topic
HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor

## What I Learned
- Working principle of the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor
- TRIG and ECHO signals
- Measuring distance using the echo pulse duration
- Using STM32 Timer for microsecond-level timing
- Converting echo pulse duration into distance
- Handling timeout conditions

## Sensor Used
HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor

## Application in EV ADAS
The ultrasonic sensor is used for obstacle detection around the vehicle.

It can provide:
- Front obstacle distance
- Left-side obstacle distance
- Right-side obstacle distance

These distance measurements are later used by the ADAS module for collision warning and blind-spot detection.
